  "slug": "host-genomic-280c",
  "summary": "Deep-learning predictors and reproducible pipelines now extract function, variants and host links from microbial metagenomes at scale.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational extraction of functional and host-relevant information from microbial genomes and metagenomes. Protein language models appear in two items: XAMP, an ESM-2/Transformer dual-engine predictor reaching AUC 0.972 that mines deep-sea metagenomes for antimicrobial peptides, and CAZyLingua, which classifies carbohydrate-active enzyme families and identifies over 27,000 CAZymes missed by other tools. Other items address reproducibility and prioritization: MeTAline provides a containerized Snakemake pipeline for shotgun profiling, SNPraefentia ranks microbial SNPs by a composite score, and Snappy performs graph-based methylation motif detection from nanopore basecalls. Host-linked annotation is represented by CAcnesDB, DISCO, the 495-model ME resource, the Fusobacterium host-read filtering pipeline, and Hi-C virus-host benchmarking. What is new is the coupling of broad enumeration with functional, structural or host context, with explicit benchmarking or validation where reported.",
